# The versions of the gate tools, in one place: check.sh installs each at its pin and runs it, on
# every machine and in CI, reading NAME=version lines (a module version, such as v1.2.3, and
# nothing else on the line), and the weekly tool-pins workflow compares each pin with the newest
# release the Go module proxy knows, opening an issue when one is behind. A pin
# moves here, by the developer's hand, in a pull request he reads: a gate's tools change only when
# we change something (developer, 2026-10-14). A change to this file runs the full check matrix.
GOLANGCI_LINT=v2.15.0
GOVULNCHECK=v1.9.0
GREMLINS=v0.6.0
GO_LICENSES=v2.0.1
